  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p data-start=\"119\" data-end=\"202\"><strong data-start=\"119\" data-end=\"153\">Total bilirubin in body fluids</strong> (commonly peritoneal or pleural) is measured to:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"204\" data-end=\"497\">\n<li data-start=\"204\" data-end=\"355\">\n<p data-start=\"206\" data-end=\"355\">Differentiate <strong data-start=\"220\" data-end=\"252\">causes of fluid accumulation</strong>, particularly in cases of suspected <strong data-start=\"289\" data-end=\"302\">bile leak</strong>, <strong data-start=\"304\" data-end=\"327\">biliary perforation</strong>, or <strong data-start=\"332\" data-end=\"355\">biliary peritonitis</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"356\" data-end=\"418\">\n<p data-start=\"358\" data-end=\"418\">Assess for <strong data-start=\"369\" data-end=\"395\">biliary tract injuries</strong> post-surgery or trauma</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"419\" data-end=\"497\">\n<p data-start=\"421\" data-end=\"497\">Evaluate <strong data-start=\"430\" data-end=\"454\">bile-stained ascites</strong> or <strong data-start=\"458\" data-end=\"479\">pleural effusions</strong> of hepatic origin</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"499\" data-end=\"584\">In normal circumstances, bilirubin levels in body fluids are <strong data-start=\"560\" data-end=\"583\">low or undetectable</strong>.</p>\n<p data-start=\"499\" data-end=\"584\">Elevated Levels &ndash; Clinical Implications :</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Condition</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Clinical Insight</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Bile leak / bile peritonitis</strong></td>\n<td>Significantly elevated fluid bilirubin; often due to trauma, surgery, or obstruction</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Spontaneous biliary rupture</strong></td>\n<td>Rare, but leads to bile-stained ascitic fluid</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Choleperitoneum / biliary fistula</strong></td>\n<td>High fluid bilirubin compared to serum levels; diagnostic in suspected fistula</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Pancreatic pseudocyst rupture into biliary tract</strong></td>\n<td>May cause bile-stained fluid with high bilirubin</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p data-start=\"499\" data-end=\"584\">&nbsp;</p>",
